  "title": "kache compiler cache in the dev container",
  "summary": "Adds kache, a Rust compiler cache, to the shared builder/reviewer dev container image. The Dockerfile downloads the pinned, checksum-verified release for the target architecture, installs it to /usr/local/bin, and writes a dev-user ~/.cargo/config.toml that sets rustc-wrapper = \"kache\" so every worktree in the container shares one compiler cache. The builder-tools smoke test now asserts both the binary and the cargo config, and the development docs describe the tool and the KACHE_DISABLED=1 escape hatch.",
